# Builder's Talent at level 2: "Whenever one or more noncreature, nonland permanents you control enter, put a +1/+1 counter
# on target creature you control." In turn 1 Bot1 makes the Talent (and its Wall), takes level 2 with the Plains and casts
# Memnite: a creature entering is no noncreature permanent, so nothing triggers (no counter, no target asked). In turn 2
# Bot2's Mox Pearl and Memnite enter under Bot2's control: not "you control", nothing triggers. In turn 3 Bot1 plays a Plains
# (a land: nothing) and then casts Mox Emerald: the trigger targets only a creature Bot1 controls, so Bot2's Memnite is
# refused and Bot1's own Memnite takes the counter, the Wall none.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Builder's Talent
Mox Emerald
Plains
Memnite
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Memnite
